          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Johann Gottfried Herder's Origins and Education</strong><br>\nJohann Gottfried Herder was born in 1744 in Mohrungen, Prussia. He was educated in theology at the University of Königsberg, where he was influenced by the philosopher Immanuel Kant.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Herder's Philosophy of Humanity</strong><br>\nHerder believed that human cultures, languages, and histories are unique and must be appreciated on their own terms. This perspective was groundbreaking and formed the foundation for modern anthropology and linguistics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Contributions to Literature and the Arts</strong><br>\nAs a literary critic, Herder's work encouraged a natural simplicity and emotion in literature, which influenced the Sturm und Drang movement. He promoted the idea that literature should express national character, drawing from folklore and oral traditions.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Herder and the Enlightenment</strong><br>\nWhile part of the Enlightenment, Herder challenged its universalist tendencies. He argued for the value of emotional experience and the importance of individual cultures, thus laying the groundwork for Romanticism.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Influence on Language and Culture</strong><br>\nHerder's ideas on the origin and evolution of language had a lasting impact. He suggested that the development of language is intertwined with the perception of the world, predating modern theories of linguistic relativity.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Idea of Volksgeist</strong><br>\nHerder introduced the concept of Volksgeist, the \"spirit of the people,\" which proposed that each nation has a distinct cultural identity shaped by language and traditions. This concept later influenced nationalistic movements.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
